{
    "$schema": "atlas-kb-curation/1",
    "$note": [
        "Atlas's editorial decisions about the prx-demo compound dump. Content is NOT here — this",
        "file carries only the judgements a machine cannot make from the source, and the import",
        "command (kb:import-compounds) reads it as a sidecar so the command itself stays generic.",
        "",
        "name/slug: the source keys on a lowercase generic_name that is neither display-quality nor",
        "URL-safe ('test cyp', 'hcg (rx)', 'aod 9604'). Slugs are fixed here rather than generated so",
        "a KB URL never moves because someone retitled a monograph.",
        "",
        "is_peptide: the gate on the peptide wiki. The source's compound_class cannot supply it — 94",
        "of 106 rows say only 'Peptide', including amoxicillin, adapalene and vitamin B12. 32 of 102",
        "compounds are actually peptides. Single amino acids (arginine, methionine) are not peptides;",
        "tripeptides (glutathione, KPV, pinealon) are.",
        "",
        "regulatory_status: seeded, not authoritative. Every monograph imports unpublished and cannot",
        "go live without a named reviewer, and confirming this field is part of what that reviewer is",
        "confirming. Where a compound has both an approved product and a research-market existence",
        "(melanotan 1 vs afamelanotide), the value describes it AS THIS PHARMACY SUPPLIES IT.",
        "",
        "merge: four pairs in the source are the same compound written twice. Two collide on slug",
        "('aod 9604'/'aod-9604'); two do not and would otherwise publish as separate monographs",
        "('5 amino 1-mq'/'5 amino 1mq' differ by a hyphen, 'mgf'/'mechano-growth-factor' and",
        "'b6'/'pyridoxine' are name-vs-synonym). 'primary' names the row whose prose survives (the",
        "longer monograph in all four cases); the absorbed row's brand names and synonyms are folded",
        "into it and its prose is discarded."
    ],
    "source_system": "prx-demo",
    "source_table": "protocol_compounds",
    "merge": [
        {
